== Writing ==

{{Main|Scripts of Hachinawa}}

Hachina was written from about 700 CE in a logographic script of its own, ''Dalewa''. From the sixteenth century the [[Zong]] script was adopted for official use and displaced the traditional characters, by the decree of the king.

== Use ==

Hachina was the language of the court, of the administration of the plain and of the temple schools. It was not the language of the empire's tributaries, who kept their own languages and their own rulers, and the correspondence of the empire with its clients was conducted in Hachina.

As the language of a state that dealt with the [[Zong]] from 1458, it acquired a body of Zong loanwords in the sixteenth century, principally in the vocabulary of administration, commerce and the objects of the trade. The loanwords entered the language in the period of the Zong script's adoption and are written in Zong characters where the Zong script is used.

